---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';

const entries = [
  {
    name: 'Guardian',
    slug: 'guardian',
    description: 'Desktop app for local inference',
    years: '2024–2025',
    stack: 'Electron, React, Node.js, SQLite, Zustand',
    outcome: 'Components reused in ForgeFrame',
    what: 'A local desktop application for examining recurring patterns in conversations, using Ollama inference and a persistent memory layer. It explored reframe detection, a user baseline, and compression of stored context.',
    decision: 'The memory engine was the useful part. Extracting it into ForgeFrame left little reason to maintain a separate desktop product, so I stopped developing the shell.',
    survived: 'The memory and tagging work moved into ForgeFrame. The questions about observation and user baselines became the essay “On Observation and Identity Modeling.”',
    lesson: 'Distinguish a separate product from an interface around infrastructure you already have.',
    demoUrl: null,
    writeupUrl: '/projects/guardian',
  },
  {
    name: 'Recursive Hall',
    slug: 'recursive-hall',
    description: 'Procedural architecture and music visualization',
    years: '2024',
    stack: 'Three.js, WebGL, GLSL, Web Audio API, JavaScript',
    outcome: 'Visual and audio components reused',
    what: 'Seeded procedural architecture rendered as wireframe drawings in one HTML file. The experiment grew to include audio-reactive shaders, a Strudel editor, a synth pad, a mixer, and a TouchDesigner bridge.',
    decision: 'I kept adding possibilities without a clear use case. Performance deteriorated, and the application became harder to reason about. I stopped expanding it and kept the parts that had a useful home elsewhere.',
    survived: 'StrudelVision took in the visual modes and audio analysis pipeline. The shader and WebGL work also informed later interface experiments.',
    lesson: 'Exploration can be worthwhile without becoming a product. It still needs a stopping point.',
    demoUrl: '/hall',
    writeupUrl: '/projects/resonance',
  },
  {
    name: 'VaultQL',
    slug: 'vaultql',
    description: 'Natural-language SQL prototype for credit unions',
    years: '2024',
    stack: 'Python, Flask, SQLCoder-34B, Ollama, Symitar Episys',
    outcome: 'Unfinished prototype',
    what: 'A prototype for querying core banking data with a local model. A schema adapter selected and annotated context for abbreviated field names, denormalized records, and integer codes. The design included role-based access, audit logs, and air-gapped inference.',
    decision: 'Too much supporting infrastructure had to be built before the query experience could be evaluated properly. I did not establish a path to a dependable deployment in a regulated environment.',
    survived: 'De-identification and context-management work carried into the ForgeFrame proxy. The domain-specific schema work remained documented, without a shipped banking product.',
    lesson: 'Domain knowledge can identify a real problem. It does not by itself establish that the product is ready to ship.',
    demoUrl: null,
    writeupUrl: null,
  },
];
---

<Page title="project archive -- alexander campos" description="Projects I stopped or folded into other work, and the decisions behind stopping.">
  <article>
    <nav class="subnav" aria-label="Misc sections">
      <a href="/misc">glossary</a>
      <a href="/misc/hall-of-shame" aria-current="page">project archive</a>
    </nav>
    <h1>Project archive</h1>
    <p class="intro">
      Projects I stopped or folded into other work. The useful record is what I tried,
      why I stopped, and which parts earned another use.
    </p>
    <div class="entries">
      {entries.map(entry => (
        <section class="entry" id={entry.slug}>
          <h2>{entry.name}</h2>
          <p class="entry-meta">{entry.description}, {entry.years}. {entry.outcome}.</p>
          <p class="entry-stack">{entry.stack}</p>
          <p>{entry.what}</p>
          <h3>Why I stopped</h3>
          <p>{entry.decision}</p>
          <h3>What carried forward</h3>
          <p>{entry.survived}</p>
          <p>{entry.lesson}</p>
          {(entry.demoUrl || entry.writeupUrl) && (
            <p class="entry-links">
              {entry.demoUrl && <a href={entry.demoUrl}>Open the experiment</a>}
              {entry.writeupUrl && <a href={entry.writeupUrl}>Read the project notes</a>}
            </p>
          )}
        </section>
      ))}
    </div>
  </article>
</Page>

<style>
  .subnav { display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .subnav a { color: var(--white-60); }
  .subnav [aria-current] { color: var(--glow-hot); }
  .intro { margin-bottom: 3rem; color: var(--white-70); }
  .entries { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3rem; }
  .entry h2 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .entry h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem; }
  .entry p { color: var(--white-70); }
  .entry .entry-meta, .entry .entry-stack { color: var(--white-60); }
  .entry-stack { font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .entry-links { display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
</style>
